## A wall crossing the left frame edge, the frame clipping it there. A vertex
## the clipper adds at the crossing takes the colour interpolated along the
## edge, so this frame's left columns match the same pixels of
## clipframe_wide.rib, whose own clip edge lies 160 columns beyond them.
## Format 640x400 with the default window [-1.6,1.6]x[-1,1] is 200 pixels
## per unit; tests/clipframeshading_test.cpp compares columns 0-119.
Display "clipframe_narrow.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 640 400 1
Projection "perspective" "fov" [40]
Clipping 0.5 60
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "ambientlight" 1 "intensity" [0.2]
LightSource "pointlight" 2 "intensity" [30] "from" [-1 0.5 4]
Sides 2
Color [0.5 0.7 0.9]
Surface "matte" "Ka" [1] "Kd" [1]
Polygon "P" [-2.5 -1.5 -4  -2.5 -1.5 20  -2.5 1.5 20  -2.5 1.5 -4]
WorldEnd
